  "note": "Election of the Warrenpoint Urban District Council, 18 September 1946. There were 18 candidates for the 12 seats. East Ward (5 seats) and West Ward (7 seats) were both polled; the Belfast News-Letter printed only the elected, and the Newry Telegraph (21 September 1946, p. 6) the full poll of both wards. The paper printed only the five successful East Ward candidates.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Belfast News-Letter, 20 September 1946, p. 3 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the note's '15 seats' -> '12 seats', as printed; names and votes confirmed. Corrected from the page image of the Newry Telegraph, 21 September 1946, p. 6 (w8-review, Nov 2026): the defeated candidate, Hugh Joseph Rice (Lab.), 191, is added, with the 447 votes cast including 4 spoiled papers; the five elected and their figures agree. The Telegraph prints George R. Shaw and George M'Alister."
